  "id": "Compound::DB00655 - Gene::1559",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Estrone and Cyp2c9, mediated through Cyp3a4 and Cyp2e1. Estrone binds to both Cyp3a4 and Cyp2e1, which are involved in oxidative metabolism of various substrates. Cyp3a4 is primarily known for its role in the oxidation of cholesterol and other lipids, while Cyp2e1 is involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid. Both enzymes are part of the Cyp2c9 pathway, indicating a shared functional role in metabolic processes. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in the relationship, with Estrone interacting with Cyp2c9 through different metabolic pathways. The mechanism involves Estrone binding to cytochrome P450 enzymes, which then catalyze the oxidation of substrates, potentially influencing drug metabolism. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of Estrone in modulating Cyp2c9 activity, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction and functional significance.",
